.TH BOOTWIRE-GUI 1 "2026-11-12" "BootWire 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bootwire\-gui \- desktop application for BootWire firmware updates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootwire\-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bootwire\-gui
opens the BootWire desktop application: firmware flashing, device profiles and
sequential batch updates, a local firmware library, diagnostics and user
commands, a frame inspector, job history, and a developer panel with verbose
output, BootWire commands and a local shell.
.PP
It is built on the same library as
.BR bootwire (1)
and keeps one target connection at a time. Choose the port
.B sim
to explore without a board.
.PP
The application needs PySide6 (Qt 6) and its Qt Quick modules. When they are
missing it prints a message and exits with status 2.
.SH FILES
Preferences, device profiles, firmware library references and job history are
stored with Qt's settings mechanism under the organisation "BootWire" and the
application "Desktop". On Linux this is
.IR ~/.config/BootWire/Desktop.conf .
.PP
The settings file of
.BR bootwire (1)
supplies the initial connection defaults; saved preferences then take
precedence.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The window was closed normally.
.TP
.B 1
The interface could not be loaded.
.TP
.B 2
The desktop dependencies are not installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bootwire (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mahmoud Abdelraouf.
